# PixiJS

- Keep Pixi objects behind a typed renderer adapter; never place them in application state.
- Reconcile immutable render descriptions into the scene graph.
- Keep world, screen, and grid coordinate transforms explicit and pure.
- Reuse containers, textures, graphics, and object pools only with measured benefit.
- Destroy owned GPU resources and detach ticker/listener callbacks on teardown.
- Do not destroy shared textures or mutate shared assets implicitly.
- Batch draw work and avoid allocations inside frame loops.
- Make z-order, culling, hit areas, and interaction modes explicit.
- Test coordinate transforms and reconciliation without a live GPU where possible.
- Degrade gracefully after renderer/context failure and surface it through an error boundary.
